<title>USA: Cyprus Amax to produce 1 bln lbs of copper in 1997.</title>
<headline>Cyprus Amax to produce 1 bln lbs of copper in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cyprus Amax Minerals is to raise its copper production by 65 percent in 1997 over its 1996 level as its El Abra mine in Chile produces at full output, the company's chief executive officer Milton Ward told analysts during a telephone conference.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be producing one billion pounds of copper in 1997, some 35 to 40 per cent of this from our low cost South American operations,&quot; Ward said.</p>
<p>Last year Cyprus produced 767 million pounds of copper.</p>
<p>Ward added that the company will produce some 700,000 ounces of gold in 1997, reaching full output by the second quarter.</p>
<p>((--New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
